---
import octicons from '@primer/octicons';
import Entry from '../components/Entry.astro';
import Full from '../layouts/Full.astro';

const icon = (name: keyof typeof octicons, size = 16) => octicons[name].toSVG({ width: size, height: size });
---

<Full
	title="Games — Avior Studio"
	description="Play termcade and Fields of Revik, and explore Castle Drop and Prizm prototypes from Avior Studio."
>
	<main id="main-content">
		<section class="page-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">
				<span></span> Games
			</p>
			<h1>
				Step into <em>another world.</em>
			</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Play the terminal arcade or enter Fields of Revik in your browser. Castle Drop and Prizm are prototypes:
				glimpses of the worlds taking shape in the studio.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="game-gallery" aria-label="Art from our games">
			<a href="https://app.revik.gg">
				<img src="/art/revik-title.png" alt="Fields of Revik" />
				<span>Play Fields of Revik ↗</span>
			</a>
			<a href="#castle-drop">
				<div class="gallery-castle">
					<img src="/art/dragon.svg" alt="Castle Drop dragon" />
				</div>
				<span>Castle Drop · prototype ↓</span>
			</a>
			<a href="#prizm">
				<div class="gallery-prizm">
					<img src="/art/crystal.svg" alt="Prizm crystal" />
				</div>
				<span>Prizm · prototype ↓</span>
			</a>
		</section>
		<section class="entries">
			<Entry
				name="termcade"
				tagline="A terminal arcade"
				status="Playable now"
				available={true}
				meta="Go · Bubble Tea · wazero"
				command="go run github.com/aviorstudio/termcade@latest"
				commandNote="Needs a truecolor terminal at 80×24 or larger"
				links={[{ href: 'https://github.com/aviorstudio/termcade', label: 'Source on GitHub' }]}
			>
				<p>
					Classic games rendered at sub-cell resolution with block pixels, so a terminal cell becomes a 2×2 or 2×3 grid
					of pixels and the playfield gets sharper than the font should allow. It ships with Asteroid, Tetris and
					Brickough, playable offline the moment it starts.
				</p>
				<p>
					The arcade compiles no games into itself. Every game is a sandboxed WebAssembly package running under wazero
					with no filesystem and no network, so a broken one shows up dimmed on the menu with its reason rather than
					taking the arcade down. The same binary is the dev kit: <code>termcade dev new you/mygame</code> scaffolds
					one, <code>termcade dev build</code>
					packages it, and anyone can publish for players to <code>termcade add</code>.
				</p>
			</Entry>

			<Entry
				name="Castle Drop"
				id="castle-drop"
				tagline="Physics-first castle defense"
				status="Prototype"
				meta="Godot 4 · private repository"
			>
				<p>
					A castle defense where the physics is the game rather than the garnish. Clear a siege, draft a tower, place it
					on a rampart slot, then use that tower's abilities to amplify what you were already doing by hand — grabbing
					attackers, throwing them, and turning enemies into collisions with each other.
				</p>
				<p>
					Progression is castle upgrades only; there is no meta-currency layer bolted on beside it. Waves, enemies,
					towers and tuning are all authored as Godot resources in the Inspector, so the balance lives in the editor
					rather than in code.
				</p>
			</Entry>

			<Entry
				name="Prizm"
				id="prizm"
				tagline="Drag-and-drop light puzzle"
				status="Prototype"
				meta="Godot 4 · private repository"
			>
				<p>
					Spend limited colour mana to cast prism spells into empty drawer slots, then drag those prisms onto the board
					so beams from the transmitters bend into the receivers that need them. Rooms are authored as scenes in the
					editor, and the beam simulation resolves each board from the pieces you have placed.
				</p>
				<p>
					Deliberately mechanics-first: no avatar to move, no combat, no health, no timer and no fail state in the MVP.
					The whole puzzle is what light does when you put something in front of it.
				</p>
			</Entry>

			<Entry
				name="Fields of Revik"
				tagline="Tactics card game"
				status="In development"
				available={true}
				meta="Godot 4 · browser game"
				links={[{ href: 'https://app.revik.gg', label: 'Play in your browser' }]}
			>
				<p>
					A tactics card game on a coloured tile board, with animal factions — outlaw raccoons, monastic bears, and more
					— whose identity comes from their mana costs rather than a faction tag, so custom decks are first-class rather
					than a mode.
				</p>
				<p>
					Offline play against the machine and online play against a person run the same rules: the deterministic
					gameplay lives in one shared core used by both the client and a headless Godot server, and online matches are
					fully server-authoritative. The client never gets to decide what happened.
				</p>
			</Entry>
		</section>

		<section class="aside-note">
			<p>
				The three Godot projects run on the studio's own devtools — GDAM pins the addons they share, gdlint checks the
				GDScript.
			</p>
			<a class="ghost-cta" href="/devtools">
				See the devtools <span class="icon" set:html={icon('arrow-right', 13)} />
			</a>
		</section>
	</main>
</Full>

<style>
	.game-gallery {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 70px;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 20px;
	}
	.game-gallery > a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}
	.game-gallery > a > img,
	.gallery-castle,
	.gallery-prizm {
		height: 320px;
		width: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: center 60%;
	}
	.game-gallery span {
		font: 11px var(--mono);
		padding: 18px 0;
	}
	.gallery-castle {
		background: #bbdce0;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
	}
	.gallery-prizm {
		background: #282c3c;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
	}
	.gallery-castle img,
	.gallery-prizm img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 95%;
		object-fit: contain;
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.game-gallery {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.game-gallery > a > img,
		.gallery-castle,
		.gallery-prizm {
			height: 350px;
		}
	}

	.page-hero {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 60px auto 70px;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 9px;
		margin: 0 0 22px;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font: 620 11px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.eyebrow span {
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--bone);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(247, 242, 233, 0.1);
	}
	/* Narrow enough that the line breaks where the sentence does, between the
		   roman half and the italic one, instead of mid-phrase. */
	h1 {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--bone);
		font-size: clamp(42px, 5.4vw, 68px);
		font-weight: 590;
		line-height: 0.99;
		letter-spacing: -0.058em;
	}
	h1 em {
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
		font-weight: 400;
	}
	.lede {
		max-width: 620px;
		margin: 28px 0 0;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.entries {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 90px;
	}

	.aside-note {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 40px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 40px;
		border-radius: 10px;
		background: var(--raised);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		padding: 34px 40px;
	}
	.aside-note p {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-size: 14.5px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	.ghost-cta {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 7px;
		flex: none;
		color: var(--paper);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
		padding: 6px 0;
		font-size: 13px;
		font-weight: 650;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.ghost-cta:hover {
		border-bottom-color: var(--paper);
	}

	@media (max-width: 980px) {
		.aside-note {
			align-items: flex-start;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 22px;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.page-hero,
		.entries,
		.aside-note {
			width: min(100% - 28px, 1180px);
		}
		.page-hero {
			margin: 36px auto 50px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: clamp(36px, 11.5vw, 52px);
		}
		.lede {
			margin-top: 22px;
			font-size: 15px;
		}
		.aside-note {
			padding: 26px 24px;
		}
		.aside-note p {
			font-size: 13.5px;
		}
	}

	h1 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: clamp(52px, 6vw, 84px);
		color: #3e5e40;
	}
	.entry-list {
		border-top: 1px solid #6a5142;
	}
</style>
